* P1 generic op amp. ORIGINAL EDUCATIONAL MODEL, NOT LM324 or a vendor model.
* Pins: noninverting, inverting, positive rail, negative rail, output.
* Finite gain, dominant pole, input resistance/bias, output resistance and limits.
* Limit before pole avoids extreme internal windup; large-signal slew is NOT
* an accurate physical model. No common-mode limits, temperature or device noise.
.subckt P1_OP inp inn vp vn out params: A0=100k GBW=1Meg VOS=0 RIN=1T IB=0 ROUT=20
Rdiff inp inn {RIN}
Ibp inp vn {IB}
Ibn inn vn {IB}
Bdrive drive 0 V=limit((V(vp)+V(vn))/2+A0*(V(inp,inn)+VOS),V(vn)+0.1,V(vp)-0.1)
Rdom drive pole 1k
Cdom pole 0 {A0/(2*pi*GBW*1k)}
Eout ideal 0 pole 0 1
Rout ideal out {ROUT}
.ends P1_OP
